    "title": "No injuries reported after flooding in Kingsport, Sullivan Co. - NewsBreak",
    "text": "KINGSPORT, Tenn. (WJHL) — No injuries were reported after flash flooding affected several parts of Kingsport on Wednesday, but two drivers had to be rescued, according to the Kingsport Fire Department (KFD). The fire department had to rescue drivers who became stranded on Riverside Avenue and Lynn Garden Drive, according to Public Information Officer Barry Brickey. The fire department also responded to a building in the 800 block of Eastern Star Road because the roof had started to cave in. A spokesperson for the Sullivan County Sheriff’s Office (SCSO) said the agency responded to 12 calls of flooding and six calls of trees down. There were also two calls initially classified as water rescues, but no one was trapped or otherwise impacted, the spokesperson said. The SCSO said several roads were closed earlier Wednesday evening due to the flash flooding. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJHL | Tri-Cities News & Weather.",
